    More precisely, $\tau'$ can be expressed with the help of the the inclusion $\times \colon \Symg_m \times \Symg_n \to \Symg_{mn}$ where the first permutation permutes blocks of size $n$ and the second permutation permutes each block. Indeed, $\tau' = (\id_3 \times \tau)(\rho \times \id_4)$ where
